import Optic
-- The part of the optics library (RD11) that does not check today. The part that does is
-- lib/Optic.wiz. Each gap is marked `-- wishful: <slug>` and described in
-- /workspace/wiz-notes/wishful/<slug>.md.

-- ## 1. Laws with ∃ and ∧ (the statement in borrows-as-optics.md §3.1)
--
-- lib/Optic.wiz states partial-lens laws with `Result.All`/`Result.Holds` and Σ types,
-- because Wiz has no `∃`/`∧`/`¬` yet. The intended statement, which a `progress`-style
-- tactic would use as rewrite rules:

structure PLens.Lawful' {S A : Type} (f : PLens S A) : Prop where   -- wishful: prop-connectives
  getPut : ∀ s a k, f s = .ok (a, k) → k a = s
  putGet : ∀ s a k a', f s = .ok (a, k) → ∃ k', f (k a') = .ok (a', k')                -- wishful: prop-connectives
  putPut : ∀ s a k a' a'' k', f s = .ok (a, k) → f (k a') = .ok (a', k') → k' a'' = k a''

-- independence of two indices of a vector (`split_at_mut`, `v.swap i j`)
def List.atL_indep {A : Type} (i j : Nat) (h : ¬ (i = j)) : PIndep (List.atL i) (List.atL j) :=   -- wishful: prop-connectives
  by induction i generalizing j <;> cases j <;> simp_all                                    -- wishful: prop-connectives

-- ## 2. The rest of `Lens.pair`'s laws
--
-- lib/Optic.wiz proves `Lens.pair_getPut` and `Lens.pair_putGet` (the latter with
-- `castRefl`, through `Optic.pairEq`). PutPut below needs rewriting under the pair:

def Lens.pair_putPut {S A B : Type} (l : Lens S A) (m : Lens S B) (hl : Lens.Lawful l) (hm : Lens.Lawful m)
    (hi : Lens.Indep l m) : Lens.PutPut (Lens.pair l m) := fun s ab cd =>
  by rw [hi.2.2, hl.2.2, hm.2.2]                                  -- wishful: unify-computed-equations

-- ## 3. `final(r)` specs (RD11: prophecy notation, desugared over the backward function)
--
-- `final(x)` in an `ensures` clause is the value of `x` when its borrow ends. For the
-- result `r : Mut ρ A S` of a function with lender `v`, `final(r)` is a fresh universally
-- quantified `fin : A`, and `final(v)` is `r.2 fin`. So
--
--   fn get_mut {'a} (v : &'a mut Vec U64) (i : USize) : &'a mut U64
--     ensures *result = old(v)[i]
--     ensures final(v) = old(v).set i final(result)
--
-- generates (and drafts/feral/lowered/03_get_mut.wiz checks, written by hand):
--
--   def get_mut.spec (v : Vec U64) (i : U64) : Prop :=
--     Result.All (fun r => (Vec.index v i = .ok r.1) × ((fin : U64) → (r.2 fin).items = …)) (get_mut v i)
--
-- The library form of the desugaring, once spec clauses exist:
def Store.Ensures {A S : Type} (st : Store A S) (P : A → A → S → Prop) : Prop :=
  (fin : A) → P st.1 fin (st.2 fin)
syntax "final" "(" ident ")" : term                                -- wishful: final-specs
-- `ensures e` where `e` mentions `final(r)`/`final(v)` ↦ `Store.Ensures r (fun cur fin v' => e[…])`

-- ## 4. Refined backward functions (dependent lenses, §1.4 / §3.4 of the note)
--
-- A borrow into a structure with an invariant must give back a value that
-- re-establishes it: the backward function takes a quantity-0 proof. This checks today
-- as a type; what is missing is the front end asking for the proof at the end of the
-- borrow (a proof obligation at the `}` where the borrow dies).
def RStore (A S : Type) (Inv : A → Prop) : Type := A × ((a : A) → (0 _ : Inv a) → S)
fn push_sorted (v : &mut SortedVec U64) (x : U64) : Unit := {     -- wishful: command-proc-macros
  let items := &mut v.items;                                       -- borrow with an invariant
  items.insert (position items x) x
} -- obligation here: sorted items                                 -- wishful: spec-clauses

-- ## 5. Traversals: the FunList spec of `iter_mut`
--
-- `traverseM` (lib/Optic.wiz) is the run-time form. Its spec form is a polynomial lens:
-- the shape goes forward, the same number of elements come back.
def FunList (A S : Type) : Type := (n : Nat) × Vec A n × (Vec A n → S)
def TraverseMut.spec {S A : Type} [TraverseMut S A] (s : S) : FunList A S := …           -- wishful: implemented-by

-- ## 6. Generated optics
--
-- For each `struct`/`enum` the front end emits field lenses, their laws and the
-- independence of distinct fields (lowered/07_disjoint.wiz has them by hand). As a
-- command macro over the reflected structure (agent/deriving's IndView):
deriving instance Lenses for Stats                                   -- wishful: command-proc-macros
-- ↦ Stats.hitsL, Stats.missesL, Stats.hitsL_lawful, …, Stats.hits_misses_indep

-- ## 7. In place without inlining: constructor contexts
--
-- `Store.comp` builds one closure per reborrow. A first-class constructor context
-- (Koka's `ctx`, a cell with a hole filled in O(1)) would make the backward function of
-- a field borrow reuse the cell without inlining. A backend feature; noted here because
-- it changes nothing in the library's types:
def Tree.leftCtx (key : U64) (right : Tree) : Ctx Tree Tree := ctx Tree.node key _ right   -- wishful: constructor-contexts
